OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,367,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36604
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F366A1785444468
OL,3,CMan set fire to childhood home after
OL,4,Cbelieving he had been cut out of will
OL,6,FThe court heard that the force of the
OL,7,Fblast put lives at risk in the
OL,8,Fresidential area.
OL,10,FCraig Davies, in a victim statement,
OL,11,Frevealed that both brothers were meant
OL,12,Fto share the house equally under their
OL,13,Fparents' will.
OL,15,FHe described the devastation of losing
OL,16,Fall his possessions, including diaries
OL,17,Fsince age 10, family photos, and
OL,18,Fjewellery, along with the home itself.
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G4/9
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,367,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36605
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F366A1785444468
OL,3,CMan set fire to childhood home after
OL,4,Cbelieving he had been cut out of will
OL,6,FHe said: "Darren has effectively
OL,7,Ferased everything that defined my life
OL,8,Fbefore 27 March."
OL,10,FCraig also spoke of the outpouring of
OL,11,Fsupport from friends, neighbours, and
OL,12,Fstrangers, saying the tragedy "brought
OL,13,Fout the best of the community."
OL,15,FDavies, who had a long history of
OL,16,Fmental health difficulties including
OL,17,Fbipolar disorder, depression, anxiety,
OL,18,Fand autism, was said to have suffered
OL,19,Fan "autism crisis" at the time of the
OL,20,Ffire.
OL,26,@nD@JOUpD@QO]tD@_OUuD@_O]{D@DOU{D@RO]
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G5/9
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,367,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36606
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F366A1785444468
OL,3,CMan set fire to childhood home after
OL,4,Cbelieving he had been cut out of will
OL,6,FHe apologised in court to his brother,
OL,7,Ffamily, neighbours, and the village,
OL,8,Facknowledging the harm caused.
OL,10,FDefending barrister Neil Ronan told
OL,11,Fthe court Davies had cared for his
OL,12,Fparents for over a decade and had
OL,13,Ffound their deaths devastating.
OL,15,FDavies had worked in the music
OL,16,Findustry before moving into telesales
OL,17,Fand had made "massive progress" in
OL,18,Fcustody thanks to psychiatric
OL,19,Ftreatment.
OL,26,@yD@NOUyD@_O]
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G6/9
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,367,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36607
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F366A1785444468
OL,3,CMan set fire to childhood home after
OL,4,Cbelieving he had been cut out of will
OL,6,FJudge Philip Parry called it a "sad
OL,7,Fand serious case," noting Davies's
OL,8,Fresponsibility was "substantially
OL,9,Freduced by your mental disorder."
OL,11,FJoanne Close from the Crown
OL,12,FProsecution Service said: "Nothing can
OL,13,Freplace the memories and belongings
OL,14,Flost in the home. His brother was left
OL,15,Fonly with the personal items he had
OL,16,Ftaken with him on his commute.
OL,18,F"Everything else he owned, and
OL,19,Feverything that had belonged to their
OL,20,Fparents, was destroyed.
OL,26,@nD@`OUoD@RO]pD@TOUqD@aO]tD@[OU
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G7/9
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,367,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36608
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F366A1785444468
OL,3,CMan set fire to childhood home after
OL,4,Cbelieving he had been cut out of will
OL,6,F"The impact on his brother has been
OL,7,Flife-changing, and he has had to rely
OL,8,Fon the kindness of the community."
OL,10,FShe added, "Other family members have
OL,11,Falso suffered the loss of treasured
OL,12,Ffamily possessions and memories."
OL,14,FDavies pleaded guilty to arson being
OL,15,Freckless as to whether life was
OL,16,Fendangered. He has been jailed for
OL,17,Ffour years and four months.
OL,19,FHe must serve half his sentence in
OL,20,Fcustody, the remainder on licence.
OL,26,@pD@bO]tD@aO]
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G8/9
